@namespace Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor

@* KildeExplorer with the open kilde in the host's address bar, and the handover to the variable
   explorer wired up. (Fhi.Metadata-zrcf4)

   Deliberately far smaller than its sibling, and that is Kelda's contract rather than a shortcut:
   KildeExplorer has no SearchChanged, no sort and no pager, so search and filters are component
   state that goes away on refresh. The one thing worth putting in a URL is which kilde is open.

   ?search= is not read, for that same reason — a link carrying it would work exactly once and
   could not be shared onward. It is left in the address bar rather than erased, along with
   everything else this component does not own.

   No class names and no markup of its own. *@

<KildeExplorer @bind-SelectedKildeId="_selectedKildeId"
               ExploreVariablesRequested="@Handover"
               Language="@Language" />
